# Scheduled-job logs written by /usr/local/bin/brawlzone-run.
#
# Caddy's access log used to share this file and now lives in
# logrotate-brawlzone-access, because it needs a different cadence: it is a
# line per request and its size is somebody else's decision, while these come
# to a few hundred kilobytes a day between them. Keeping them together meant
# the hourly timer added on 2026-09-28 rotated these hourly too, fragmenting
# them and leaving `brawlzone-log <job>` showing an empty file.
#
# copytruncate because a job may be mid-run when logrotate fires: the wrapper
# holds the file open, so renaming it would leave systemd writing to an
# unlinked inode and the rest of that run would vanish.
#
# One directory per job; the archives rotate beside the log they belong to.

# `[!a]*` rather than `*`, because logrotate refuses a file that two stanzas
# both match -- including stanzas in different files under logrotate.d, so
# splitting the access log out did not remove the need for this. The access
# directory is owned by logrotate-brawlzone-access; the one other directory
# starting with "a" is named back in explicitly.
/var/log/brawlzone/[!a]*/*.log /var/log/brawlzone/alert/*.log {
    daily
    maxsize 100M
    rotate 30
    missingok
    notifempty
    compress
    copytruncate
    dateext
    dateformat -%Y-%m-%d-%s
    su root adm
    create 0664 root adm
}
